# Never merge to master

Never merge into `master` or `main`. The user lands every change there by hand.

The word "merge" never means merge to `master` or `main`. "Merge", "push and merge", "merge it", and "merge the PR" approve work on the feature branch only.

Do not run any of these:

- `gh pr merge` (squash, merge, or rebase)
- `git merge` into `master` or `main`
- `git push` of `master` or `main`, including a revert, fixup, or "undo" of a merge

Push the feature branch and stop. Leave the pull request open. Say that it is ready for the user to merge.
